From: FlipperOneEmu
Subject: [PATCH] accel/tcg/mttcg: an interrupt without an exit request

An interrupt that another thread raises for an MTTCG vCPU (a timer's,
a device's, another CPU's SGI) kicked it as a pause does: an exit
request, after which cpu_exec returns, and the vCPU's thread takes the
BQL to look at its events before it enters cpu_exec again. An interrupt
needs less: a halted vCPU woken, a running one out of its chain of TBs
to cpu_exec's interrupt check. (The kick's own comment says as much:
"this is not always needed".) Counted with Flipper OS booting on the
RK3576's eight cores: cpu_exec returned for an exit request 11,000 to
35,000 times a second, half of them with no work queued for the vCPU.

Now, under MTTCG, an interrupt wakes the vCPU's halt condition and sets
icount_decr's high half, as an interrupt the vCPU raises for itself
already did, and no more. A pause, queued work and exclusive sections
still kick with an exit request. Round-robin TCG and icount are as
before.

---
--- a/accel/tcg/tcg-accel-ops-mttcg.h	2026-11-26 09:34:17.409695595 -0500
+++ b/accel/tcg/tcg-accel-ops-mttcg.h	2026-11-26 09:34:17.464520217 -0500
@@ -13,4 +13,7 @@
 /* start an mttcg vCPU thread */
 void mttcg_start_vcpu_thread(CPUState *cpu);
 
+/* an interrupt for a vCPU: to its interrupt check, without an exit request */
+void mttcg_handle_interrupt(CPUState *cpu, int mask);
+
 #endif /* TCG_ACCEL_OPS_MTTCG_H */
--- a/accel/tcg/tcg-accel-ops-mttcg.c	2026-11-26 09:34:17.417177879 -0500
+++ b/accel/tcg/tcg-accel-ops-mttcg.c	2026-11-26 09:34:17.464734374 -0500
@@ -122,6 +122,25 @@
     return NULL;
 }
 
+/*
+ * An interrupt for a vCPU. Halted, it is woken; running, it leaves its
+ * chain of TBs at the next one, for cpu_exec's interrupt check, which is
+ * all that an interrupt needs. Not the kick's exit request
+ * (tcg_kick_vcpu_thread()): that makes cpu_exec return, and the vCPU's
+ * thread take the BQL to look at its events before it goes on, for each
+ * interrupt that another thread raises (the timers', the devices', the
+ * other CPUs' SGIs).
+ */
+void mttcg_handle_interrupt(CPUState *cpu, int mask)
+{
+    cpu_set_interrupt(cpu, mask);
+    if (!qemu_cpu_is_self(cpu)) {
+        qemu_cond_broadcast(cpu->halt_cond);
+    }
+    /* (after the request: cpu_exec sees it, or this, and looks again) */
+    qatomic_store_release(&cpu->neg.icount_decr.u16.high, -1);
+}
+
 void mttcg_start_vcpu_thread(CPUState *cpu)
 {
     char thread_name[VCPU_THREAD_NAME_SIZE];
--- a/accel/tcg/tcg-accel-ops.c	2026-11-26 09:34:17.426413923 -0500
+++ b/accel/tcg/tcg-accel-ops.c	2026-11-26 09:34:17.464939616 -0500
@@ -203,7 +203,7 @@
     if (qemu_tcg_mttcg_enabled()) {
         ops->create_vcpu_thread = mttcg_start_vcpu_thread;
         ops->kick_vcpu_thread = tcg_kick_vcpu_thread;
-        ops->handle_interrupt = tcg_handle_interrupt;
+        ops->handle_interrupt = mttcg_handle_interrupt;
     } else {
         ops->create_vcpu_thread = rr_start_vcpu_thread;
         ops->kick_vcpu_thread = rr_kick_vcpu_thread;
